Everything is configured correctly. Here's a summary of what was set up:

**Directory: `/srv/shared`**
- **Owner:** root, **Group:** research
- **Permissions:** 2770 (rwxrws---) — setgid bit ensures new files/dirs inherit the `research` group

**Current ACLs:**
| Entry | Permissions |
|---|---|
| user::rwx | owner (root) full access |
| user:alice:rwx | alice full access |
| user:bob:rwx | bob full access |
| group::rwx | owning group full access |
| group:research:rwx | research group full access |
| mask::rwx | mask allows full permissions |
| other::--- | no access for others |

**Default ACLs (inherited by new files/subdirs):**
| Entry | Permissions |
|---|---|
| default:user::rwx | |
| default:user:alice:rwx | alice inherits full access |
| default:user:bob:rwx | bob inherits full access |
| default:group::rwx | |
| default:group:research:rwx | research group inherits full access |
| default:mask::rwx | mask allows full permissions |
| default:other::--- | others get no access |

This ensures that any file or subdirectory created by alice or bob inside `/srv/shared` will automatically inherit ACLs granting both users full rwx access, while users outside the research group are completely blocked.

